.\" Man page for esm.do CLI
.\" Contact support@esm.do for errors or questions
.TH ESM 1 "January 2025" "esm.do 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
esm \- Living ESM module management for AI agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esm
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B esm
is a command-line interface for managing ESM modules on esm.do.
It allows you to create, read, write, test, and run modules
with full version control and sandboxed execution.
.PP
Every module consists of four synchronized files:
.IP \(bu 2
.B index.d.ts
\- TypeScript type definitions
.IP \(bu 2
.B index.mjs
\- ESM module implementation
.IP \(bu 2
.B index.test.js
\- Vitest-compatible tests
.IP \(bu 2
.B index.script.js
\- Executable script
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Module Management"
.TP
.B init \fIname\fP
Initialize a new module with the given name.
Names must be in @scope/name format.
.TP
.B write \fIname\fP
Write content to a module. Creates the module if it doesn't exist.
.TP
.B read \fIname\fP
Read the content of a module.
.TP
.B delete \fIname\fP
Delete a module (requires \-\-force flag).
.SS "Execution"
.TP
.B run \fIname\fP
Execute the module's script in a sandboxed environment.
.TP
.B test \fIname\fP
Run the module's tests using the built-in test framework.
.SS "Version Control"
.TP
.B versions \fIname\fP
List version history for a module.
.TP
.B log \fIname\fP
Show commit history for a module.
.TP
.B diff \fIname\fP \fIv1\fP [\fIv2\fP]
Compare two versions of a module.
.SS "Authentication"
.TP
.B login
Authenticate with esm.do.
.TP
.B logout
Log out and remove stored credentials.
.TP
.B whoami
Display the current authenticated user.
.SS "Configuration"
.TP
.B config get \fIkey\fP
Get a configuration value.
.TP
.B config set \fIkey\fP \fIvalue\fP
Set a configuration value.
.TP
.B config list
List all configuration values.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Global Options"
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help for the command.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the CLI version.
.SS "init Options"
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-template " " \fItemplate\fP
Template to use (default, typescript). Default: default
.SS "write Options"
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " " \fIpath\fP
Read module code from file.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-content " " \fIcontent\fP
Module code as string.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-message " " \fImessage\fP
Commit message.
.TP
.B \-\-stdin
Read content from stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-types \fItypes\fP
TypeScript type definitions.
.TP
.B \-\-module \fImodule\fP
Module code (JavaScript).
.TP
.B \-\-tests \fItests\fP
Test code.
.TP
.B \-\-script \fIscript\fP
Executable script.
.SS "read Options"
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version " " \fIversion\fP
Read specific version by hash.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIfile\fP
Write output to file.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output as JSON (includes all components).
.SS "run Options"
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " " \fIms\fP
Execution timeout in milliseconds. Default: 30000
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-env " " \fIKEY=value\fP
Environment variables (can be repeated).
.SS "test Options"
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-watch
Watch mode (re-run on changes).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-coverage
Collect coverage information.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-filter " " \fIpattern\fP
Filter tests by name pattern.
.SS "versions Options"
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-limit " " \fIn\fP
Maximum versions to show. Default: 10
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-verbose
Show detailed info (message, date).
.SS "log Options"
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-limit " " \fIn\fP
Maximum entries to show. Default: 10
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-verbose
Show full commit details.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-since " " \fIdate\fP
Show commits since date.
.SS "diff Options"
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-unified " " \fIn\fP
Context lines in unified diff. Default: 3
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output as JSON.
.SS "delete Options"
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Skip confirmation prompt.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be deleted.
.SS "login Options"
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-token " " \fItoken\fP
API token for authentication.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS "Initialize a new module"
.nf
.RS
esm init @myorg/calculator
esm init @myorg/utils --template typescript
.RE
.fi
.SS "Write module content"
.nf
.RS
esm write @myorg/math --file ./math.js
esm write @myorg/math --content "export const PI = 3.14159"
esm write @myorg/math \\
  --types "export declare function add(a: number, b: number): number" \\
  --module "export function add(a, b) { return a + b }"
.RE
.fi
.SS "Read module content"
.nf
.RS
esm read @myorg/math
esm read @myorg/math --json
esm read @myorg/math --version abc123
esm read @myorg/math --output ./local-math.js
.RE
.fi
.SS "Run tests"
.nf
.RS
esm test @myorg/math
esm test @myorg/math --filter "add"
esm test @myorg/math --coverage
.RE
.fi
.SS "Execute scripts"
.nf
.RS
esm run @myorg/calculator
esm run @myorg/api-client --env API_KEY=abc123
esm run @myorg/cli -- --input file.txt
.RE
.fi
.SS "View history"
.nf
.RS
esm versions @myorg/math
esm log @myorg/math --verbose
esm diff @myorg/math abc123 def456
.RE
.fi
.SS "Authentication"
.nf
.RS
esm login --token your-api-token
esm whoami
esm logout
.RE
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ESM_TOKEN
Authentication token (overrides config file).
.TP
.B ESM_API_ENDPOINT
API base URL (overrides config file).
.TP
.B ESM_CONFIG_PATH
Path to configuration file.
.TP
.B DEBUG
Set to "esm:*" to enable debug output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.esm/config.json
User configuration file containing API endpoint and authentication token.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (module not found, tests failed, etc.).
.SH MODULE NAMING
Module names must be in scoped format: @scope/name
.PP
Examples of valid names:
.IP \(bu 2
@myorg/utils
.IP \(bu 2
@personal/calculator
.IP \(bu 2
@company/api/v2/client
.PP
The scope is typically an organization, username, or project name.
Nested paths are allowed for organizing related modules.
.SH SECURITY
.TP
.B Sandboxed Execution
All module scripts and tests run in isolated V8 contexts
with limited capabilities. Network access and file system
access are restricted.
.TP
.B Token Security
API tokens should be treated as secrets. Use environment
variables in CI/CD pipelines and never commit tokens to
version control.
